 {
  "id": "dedupe_records",
  "function": "dedupe_records",
  "spec": "dedupe_records(records, key) removes duplicate records from a list of dicts. Two records are duplicates when both have the field `key` and the values are equal (1 and '1' are different values; None equals None). For each group of duplicates the result keeps one record: the content of the LAST record of the group, placed at the position where the FIRST record of the group appeared. Records that lack the field `key` are never duplicates of anything and are all kept in place. Return a new list.",
  "examples": [
   "dedupe_records([{'id': 1, 'v': 'a'}, {'id': 1, 'v': 'b'}], 'id') == [{'id': 1, 'v': 'b'}]",
   "dedupe_records([], 'id') == []"
  ],
